/* The exact opposite bug, same root cause: a `text-white` sitting on a
   hard-coded purple/blue gradient FILL (the VPS plan-selection step's
   "Selected" button, its "Most popular" ribbon, the storage quick-picks, the
   hosting-plan ribbon) wants literal white always — the fill never changes
   with the theme, only the token does. In dark mode that is invisible (both
   are `#fff`), but in light mode `--color-white` is deliberately flipped to
   near-black ink for ordinary headings, and this button caught that flip too:
   black text on a purple button. A handful of these spots already dodge it by
